{
  "_comment": "Weapons and warheads. range and splash are in tiles; cooldown in ticks (15 per second); speed in leptons per tick (256 = 1 tile). Warhead values are percent damage against each armour class; armour-piercing rounds come in three weights (ap_light: 37-45 mm and anti-tank rifles, ap: 57-76 mm and rocket teams, ap_heavy: 85 mm and up, long 75s and 17-pounders) and only the heavy ones go through a heavy tank's front at full effect; 'facing' is percent damage by the side of a vehicle that is struck (front / side / rear), so flanking pays. accuracy is the percent chance an instant-hit weapon hits (rifles miss 30% of the time: green troops). A gun's 'vsInfantry' names the round it switches to against soldiers. burst: shells fired at once per shot (rocket salvoes), scattered over burstSpread tiles. sound / impact (presentation only): the firing sound and the sound where it lands, names from content/audio/audio.json; left out, they are chosen by the kind of weapon and its warhead.",
